        "original_id": "a571aa39-c201-5229-b43f-97124b8f312d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Rio Airways, Dal Airways, Hood Airways\n- Places: Killeen, Texas, Dallas Love Field, Dallas, Texas, Dallas/Fort Worth International Airport\n- Topics: regional passenger airlines, commuter air carriers, airport operations\n\nFacts:\n- Rio Airways was a regional passenger airline headquartered in Killeen, Texas, United States, and it operated from 1967 to 1987.\n- Rio Airways had its roots in the smaller commuter air carriers Dal Airways and Hood Airways.\n- Dallas Love Field was Dallas' main airport until Dallas/Fort Worth International Airport opened in 1974.\n- Prior to operating at Dallas/Fort Worth International Airport, Rio Airways operated at Dallas Love Field.\n- Dallas Love Field is a city-owned public airport located 6 miles northwest of downtown Dallas, Texas.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "066dc9d2-361d-5526-a9d1-fbf1331d497f",
        "text": "Page: Rio Airways. Sentence: Rio Airways was a regional passenger airline headquartered in Killeen, Texas, United States, which was operational from 1967 to 1987.\nPage: Rio Airways. Sentence: Prior to operations at DFW it operated at Dallas Love Field, having its roots in two smaller commuter air carriers, Dal Airways and Hood Airways.\nPage: Dallas Love Field. Sentence: Dallas Love Field (IATA: DAL, ICAO: KDAL, FAA LID: DAL) is a city-owned public airport 6 miles (10 km) northwest of downtown Dallas, Texas.\nPage: Dallas Love Field. Sentence: It was Dallas' main airport until 1974 when Dallas/Fort Worth International Airport (DFW) opened.",
